UPDATE lessons SET title='Year 3, Week 15, Lesson 1: Adding and subtracting fractions with the same denominator', data=json_patch(data,'{"child_mission":"Adding or subtracting fractions with the same denominator means joining or removing equal-sized parts; the denominator stays the same while numerators combine.","coming_soon":null,"duration_minutes":55,"evidence_instructions":"Save the independent response, specific revisions and both short-answer explanations; record oral evidence for speaking tasks.","explicit_teaching":null,"extension":"Apply the same method to a larger number or a new context, then compare two solution paths for accuracy.","follow_up_challenges":null,"guided_practice":"PRACTISE BEFORE READING THE FEEDBACK\nCompute 3/8 + 2/8 and 5/6 − 1/6. Simplify if you know an equivalent.\n\nFEEDBACK\n5/8; 4/6 (=2/3 if recognised).\n\nWATCH FOR\nAdding denominators (2/5+1/5=3/10) invents a new part size incorrectly.","hoard_words":null,"independent_task":"INDEPENDENT EVIDENCE\nSolve twelve +/− problems with common denominators. Show a bar or number-line sketch for four of them. Simplify two answers using equivalence.\n\nWrite a short reflection naming one step you corrected and why.","interactive_activities":null,"learning_area":"Mathematics","learning_intention":"Adding or subtracting fractions with the same denominator means joining or removing equal-sized parts; the denominator stays the same while numerators combine.","lesson_number":1,"lesson_role":"Concept","materials":["Paper or typed answer space","Pencil","Optional: place-value chart or number line"],"offline_alternative":"Use paper and pencil to complete the original task, then retain a photograph or short parent observation as evidence.","outcome_codes":["MA2-PF-01"],"parent_notes":"Parent: Marking guidance for the independent task: Solve twelve +/− problems with common denominators. Show a bar or number-line sketch for four of them. Simplify two answers using equivalence. Accept equivalent origina