ction, make your own attempt using the exact question provided. Compare your working with the feedback: did you use the same skill and show your reasoning? If a digit or place is uncertain, identify what would have to be regrouped or counted again. One deliberate, justified revision is more useful than writing a longer answer.","icon":"📖","notice":"Writing only the final answer without working does not show the method. Correct the value or method, not just the appearance of the digits.","title":"Show the working","visual":[{"alt":"Correct subtraction contrasted with denominator-add error.","caption":"Part size does not change when joining like parts.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#e8f5ed\" stroke=\"#297a61\"/><g font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#263948\"><text x=\"28\" y=\"42\">Subtract</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"78\">3/4 − 1/4 = 2/4</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"42\">Error</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"78\">adding denominators</text></g></svg>"}]},{"check":{"correct_index":3,"explanation":"Use an intentionally incorrect attempt as a comparison.","options":["A calculation unrelated to the numbers given","An answer copied without understanding","A guess with no working","Use an intentionally incorrect attempt as a comparison"],"question":"Which choice best applies this lesson idea about add with clear evidence?","type":"multiple_choice"},"example":"WORKED MODEL\nAdding denominators (2/5+1/5=3/10) invents a new part size incorrectly. Here is a more productive model: 2/5 + 1/5 = 3/5. 3/4 − 1/4 = 2/4 (which equals 1/2). Denominator 5 (or 4) names the part size.\n\nTRY FIRST\nDescribe why the warned-against approach gives the wrong value or meaning, then write corrected working.\n\nFEEDBACK\n5/8; 4/6 (=2/3 if recognised).","explain":"Use an intentionally incorrect attempt as a c